<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nguyen Thi Binh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1927</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nguyen Thi Binh is a Vietnamese communist politician who served as foreign minister of the Provisional Revolutionary Government of the Republic of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. She led its delegation at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> peace talks and was the only woman to sign the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-accords">Paris Peace Accords</a> of 1973. After reunification she became minister of education and vice-president of Vietnam from 1992 to 2002.</p></div>
